From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x23x-ha <190664518+x23x-ha@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:38:49 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: b43: N-PHY: don't set chip control bit 6 on the
 BCM43217

b43_phy_initn() sets bit 6 of chipcommon chip control on every N-PHY
rev 3+ with an external 2.4 GHz LNA. On the BCM43217 that bit cuts the
second core's RX by about 30 dB: on an ASUS RT-AC1200G+ the per-chain
RSSI was -49/-80 with b43, while the vendor firmware leaves the bit
clear and gets -44/-41. Setting the bit by hand under the vendor driver
drops core 1 to -73/-75; clearing it brings it back.

Clear the bit on the BCM43217 instead of setting it.

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
index 1c9325d..75c02bc 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
@@ -7254,14 +7254,23 @@ static int b43_phy_initn(struct b43_wldev *dev)
 	u16 clip[2];
 	bool do_cal = false;
 
+	/*
+	 * Not on the BCM43217: there chip control bit 6 cuts core 1's RX by
+	 * ~30 dB (vendor firmware leaves it clear; setting it by hand under
+	 * the vendor driver gives the same loss). Clear it there instead.
+	 */
 	if ((dev->phy.rev >= 3) &&
 	   (sprom->boardflags_lo & B43_BFL_EXTLNA) &&
 	   (b43_current_band(dev->wl) == NL80211_BAND_2GHZ)) {
 		switch (dev->dev->bus_type) {
 #ifdef CPTCFG_B43_BCMA
 		case B43_BUS_BCMA:
-			bcma_cc_set32(&dev->dev->bdev->bus->drv_cc,
-				      BCMA_CC_CHIPCTL, 0x40);
+			if (dev->dev->chip_id == BCMA_CHIP_ID_BCM43217)
+				bcma_cc_mask32(&dev->dev->bdev->bus->drv_cc,
+					       BCMA_CC_CHIPCTL, ~0x40);
+			else
+				bcma_cc_set32(&dev->dev->bdev->bus->drv_cc,
+					      BCMA_CC_CHIPCTL, 0x40);
 			break;
 #endif
 #ifdef CPTCFG_B43_SSB
